Derivation chain
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This work is a derivative of the following projects, each of which is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Every link in the chain is a GitHub fork
of the one above it.

1. cert-manager/webhook-example
   https://github.com/cert-manager/webhook-example
   Copyright The cert-manager Authors.
   The original ACME DNS01 webhook solver scaffold: the `webhook.Solver`
   implementation shape, the Helm chart layout (apiservice, pki, rbac, service
   and deployment templates, and _helpers.tpl), and the conformance test
   harness all originate here.

2. bcspragu/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun
   https://github.com/bcspragu/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun
   Added the Porkbun integration: the Porkbun API client and the Present /
   CleanUp logic that maps ACME challenges onto Porkbun DNS records.

3. Talinx/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun
   https://github.com/Talinx/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun
   Packaged the project: the Helm chart under charts/, the GitHub Actions
   workflows for publishing the image and chart, and the 1.0.0 release. This
   repository is a direct fork of that work.

The upstream README also credits baarde/cert-manager-webhook-ovh
(https://github.com/baarde/cert-manager-webhook-ovh, Apache-2.0) as an
inspiration for the original Porkbun integration. That attribution is carried
forward here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Related independent fork
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pabloa/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun
https://github.com/pabloa/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun

A separate, actively released fork of Talinx/cert-manager-webhook-porkbun. It
independently identified the same registered-domain-versus-DNS-zone problem
addressed here, and solves it differently (probing the Porkbun API for
candidate zones rather than consulting the public suffix list).

No code from that fork is incorporated into this one; the two were developed
independently from the same Talinx ancestor. It is listed here as
acknowledgement of prior art, not as a source of this work.

